### 3.2 Barrel Electro - Magnetic Calorimeter (BEMC)

The BEMC is a lead-scintillator sampling electromagnetic calorimeter [96] which is located inside the aluminium coil of the STAR solenoid and covers \(|\eta|\leq 1.0\) and \(2\pi\) in azimuth and thus matches in acceptance with the TPC tracking. Figure (3.32) shows the cross-sectional view of the STAR detector with BEMC.

