In Figure (6.18), we present the energy dependence of the three HBT radii, the ratio of \(R_{out}/R_{side}\) for the available data from AGS, SPS and RHIC energies. The results are compiled for Au+Au, Pb+Pb and Pb+Au collisions at mid-rapidity and for \(<k_{T}>\)\(\sim\) 0.2-0.3 GeV/c. With this we have included our measurements in Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{\rm NN}}\) = 62.4 GeV. The quality of the data and the error bars show significant improvement for the present STAR results compared to those obtained before for PHOBOS [209] at the same energy. The HBT radii do not show any sharp rise from SPS to RHIC energies.

